WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:04.740
With so many rumors and news tidbits floating
around, It can be tough keeping track of what's

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:06.920
going on in the MCU, and what's coming up.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:10.790
Well, strap on your Vibranium shield, because
we're hitting you with every project you can

00:00:10.790 --> 00:00:13.839
expect to see in Phase 4 of the Marvel Cinematic
Universe.

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:19.220
We've been promised it would happen for years,
and on May 1, 2020, it finally will.

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:23.680
Black Widow, in which Scarlett Johansson will
reprise the role of superspy Natasha Romanoff

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:25.580
for what very well might be the last time.

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:29.980
The prequel is set in the period between Civil
War and Infinity War, but will likely also

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:32.860
flash back to the time before Romanoff's recruitment
by S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:37.399
According to director Cate Shortland, the
flick will find Romanoff in a dark place,

00:00:37.399 --> 00:00:41.261
following her as she, quote, "[puts] the pieces
of herself together and [comes] out a whole

00:00:41.261 --> 00:00:41.900
person."

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:46.260
Much of the action will take place overseas,
and yes, we may finally get to find out just

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:47.260
what went down in Budapest.

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:49.500
"Just like Budapest all over again."

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:52.340
"You and I remember Budapest very differently."

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:57.120
Johansson's co-stars include Florence Pugh
and Rachel Weisz, who will appear as operatives

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:00.840
who have undergone the same Red Room training
that honed Romanoff's deadly skills.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:05.580
Also starring is David Harbour, who will portray
the Red Guardian, Russia's answer to Captain

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:06.080
America.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:10.860
Rounding out the cast will be O-T Fagbenle
as Marcus, an underworld "fixer," and Ray

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:12.570
Winstone, whose role is undisclosed.

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:16.580
It's not yet known who will be playing the
flick's reported villain, Taskmaster, whose

00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:20.880
photographic reflexes allow him to perfectly
mimic the fighting style of anyone he faces.

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:27.140
Another long-rumored project to receive final
confirmation at San Diego Comic-Con 2019 was

00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:30.970
the Disney+ limited series The Falcon and
the Winter Soldier, which will see Anthony

00:01:30.970 --> 00:01:35.340
Mackie and Sebastian Stan reprising their
roles of Steve Rogers' two best buddies who

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:37.500
just happen to kind of hate one another.

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:39.200
"Can you move your seat up?"

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:40.120
"No."

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:45.220
Perhaps the announcement's biggest reveal
is its logo, which sports a very Captain America-esque

00:01:45.220 --> 00:01:45.720
design.

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:49.940
It seems that Sam Wilson will have a bit of
reconciling to do between his old heroic identity

00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:54.420
and the new identity, bequeathed to him by
Rogers himself at the conclusion of Avengers:

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:54.920
Endgame.

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:59.340
Plot details have so far been kept under wraps,
but we do know one thing: the six-episode

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:03.890
series will see the return of Zemo, the man
who goaded the Avengers into the titular conflict

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:07.820
of Captain America: Civil War, and he'll be
sporting his distinctive purple mask from

00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:08.320
the comics.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:13.180
Kari Skogland will direct every episode, with
writing duties being handled by Malcolm Spellman

00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:14.280
and Derek Kolstad.

00:02:14.450 --> 00:02:19.040
The series won't be part of the original offerings
Disney+ will feature at launch, but is expected

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:21.880
to hit the streamer sometime in mid- to late
2020.

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:27.060
Marvel Studios opened their Comic-Con panel
with discussion of The Eternals, an interesting

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:31.650
if lesser-known property which should help
anchor the Cosmic side of the MCU moving forward.

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:36.020
The titular race of superpowered beings were
created eons ago by the Celestials to defend

00:02:36.020 --> 00:02:38.200
the Earth from their polar opposites the Deviants.

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:42.540
Marvel head honcho Kevin Feige has teased
that The Eternals' story may span, quote,

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:46.519
"tens of thousands of years," telling an epic
story of the type we haven't yet seen in the

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:47.020
MCU.

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:51.240
The movie, which will be directed by The Rider
helmer Chloe Zhao, has assembled a suitably

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:53.900
epic cast for its November 6, 2020, release.

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:58.870
The Eternals will star Richard Madden as Ikaris,
Alongside him is Angelina Jolie as Thena,

00:02:58.870 --> 00:03:04.650
Kumail Nanjiani as Kingo, Lauren Ridloff as
Makkari, Brian Tyree Henry as Phastos, Salma

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:07.940
Hayek as Ajak, and Lia McHugh as the trickster
Sprite.

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:13.120
The starring vehicle for the MCU's first Asian
superhero movie protagonist Shang-Chi, Master

00:03:13.129 --> 00:03:18.200
of Kung Fu, was teased in late 2018, but until
the title was revealed at San Diego Comic-Con

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:21.469
in July 2019, its iconic villain had only
been rumored.

00:03:21.469 --> 00:03:25.390
It turned out that the rumors were true: Shang-Chi
and the Legend of the Ten Rings will see the

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:29.590
supremely skilled fighter facing off against
the Mandarin, the classic Iron Man villain

00:03:29.590 --> 00:03:34.200
who had been cruelly teased with Ben Kingsley's
impostor, actor Trevor Slattery, in Iron Man

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:34.700
3.

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:35.880
"Don't hurt the face!

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:36.720
I'm an actor!"

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:39.780
"You've got a minute to live, fill it with
words."

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:43.489
Of course, the Marvel One-Shot All Hail the
King revealed that the real deal was still

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:46.540
out there somewhere, and now, he'll finally
make his presence known.

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:50.549
It seems that the Ten Rings, the terrorist
organization who kidnapped Tony Stark in Iron

00:03:50.549 --> 00:03:54.579
Man, will figure prominently into the screen
origin of Shang-Chi, who in the comics is

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:57.220
perhaps the finest unarmed combatant in existence.

00:03:57.430 --> 00:04:02.200
Destin Daniel Cretton has been tapped to direct,
with Chinese Canadian actor Simu Liu holding

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:03.240
down the title role.

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:07.879
Also confirmed to be starring are Awkwafina
in an undisclosed role and legendary Chinese

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:09.840
actor Tony Leung as the Mandarin.

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:14.000
Rumors have already begun swirling that the
nefarious baddie will be retconned as Shang-Chi's

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:16.570
father in the flick, but for now, this is
unconfirmed.

00:04:16.820 --> 00:04:20.040
We'll find out when it's released February
12, 2021.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:25.000
When it was first announced in late 2018 that
Marvel Studios would be developing multiple

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:29.180
limited series for the Disney+ streaming service,
it didn't take long to get confirmation on

00:04:29.180 --> 00:04:33.280
the first of these: a show about Loki, which
will see Tom Hiddleston returning to portray

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:35.000
the beloved trickster god once more.

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:39.340
While plot details remain scarce, Hiddleston
did appear during Marvel Studios' panel at

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:44.280
San Diego Comic-Con to confirm a spring 2021
release for Loki, hinting that the series

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:48.090
will answer fans' questions about where the
Avengers-era Loki went with the Tesseract

00:04:48.090 --> 00:04:50.360
after disappearing during Endgame's time heist.

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:53.879
Of course, the character met a grim end at
the hands of Thanos in the brutal opening

00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:58.240
sequence of Avengers: Infinity War, and his
death is expected to actually take this time.

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:03.040
According to The Hollywood Reporter, the series
will follow Loki as he, quote, "pops up throughout

00:05:03.050 --> 00:05:07.370
human history as an unlikely influencer on
historical events," like a less-friendly,

00:05:07.370 --> 00:05:08.479
time traveling Forrest Gump.

00:05:08.479 --> 00:05:12.110
The project has scored a showrunner who should
know his way around this kind of material:

00:05:12.110 --> 00:05:15.919
Michael Waldron, who has worked as a writer
on Adult Swim's Rick and Morty and will be

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:19.880
credited as creator and executive producer,
in addition to writing the pilot.

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:24.420
It's an inspired premise and a spot-on creative
choice, but let's face it: Disney+ had us

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:26.420
at "Tom Hiddleston will return as Loki."

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:31.000
"This universe is only one of an infinite
number.

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:35.020
Worlds without end."

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:40.860
2016's Doctor Strange gave us the MCU's first
look at the Multiverse, so it was only to

00:05:40.879 --> 00:05:44.759
be expected that the sequel, which has been
in the works since before the first film even

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:46.760
released, should further explore the concept.

00:05:46.760 --> 00:05:51.040
But this time around, it appears that traversing
multiple alternate realities will be central

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:56.389
to the plot, as evidenced by the flick's title,
revealed at San Diego Comic-Con 2019: Doctor

00:05:56.389 --> 00:05:58.340
Strange in the Multiverse of Madness.

00:05:58.440 --> 00:06:02.720
Returning director Scott Derrickson was previously
most at home in the horror genre, having helmed

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:05.620
such flicks as The Exorcism of Emily Rose
and Sinister.

00:06:05.770 --> 00:06:09.460
For the further adventures of Stephen Strange,
Derrickson has promised that he'll deliver,

00:06:09.479 --> 00:06:15.150
quote, "the first scary MCU film," on May
7, 2021, which sounds like an amazing prospect.

00:06:15.150 --> 00:06:19.531
But wait, there's more: fans at SDCC were
also treated to the announcement that the

00:06:19.531 --> 00:06:24.189
movie would co-star Elizabeth Olsen as Wanda
Maximoff/Scarlet Witch, along with her potent

00:06:24.189 --> 00:06:26.140
and dangerous reality-warping powers.

00:06:26.250 --> 00:06:30.660
It was also revealed that the film would tie
directly into the plot of the upcoming Disney+

00:06:30.669 --> 00:06:35.130
series WandaVision, which will see Olsen reprise
the role along with Paul Bettany as a probably

00:06:35.130 --> 00:06:36.080
less gray Vision.

00:06:36.380 --> 00:06:40.300
We expected to see further team-ups along
the lines of the Thor/Hulk pairing in Thor:

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:44.580
Ragnarok for Phase 4, and we must say that
this one was quite unexpected, and inspired.

00:06:45.580 --> 00:06:49.580
Among the more intriguing Disney+ limited
series is WandaVision, which will be run by

00:06:49.580 --> 00:06:54.360
Captain Marvel writer Jac Schaeffer and will
feature the reunion of Scarlet Witch and Vision.

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:58.320
Of course, everyone's favorite robot boyfriend
was looking just a tad bit dead the last time

00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:02.160
we saw him, during the climax of Avengers:
Infinity War, and he didn't return in the

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:02.660
"blip."

00:07:02.660 --> 00:07:06.360
While it's not known exactly how the Avenging
android will make his return, there are a

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:08.620
few bread crumbs we can follow that give us
a clue.

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:13.560
Elizabeth Olsen has said that at least a portion
of the series takes place in the 1950s, which

00:07:13.561 --> 00:07:18.040
doesn't make a great deal of sense unless
perhaps time travel is involved, or, perhaps,

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:18.700
alternate realities.

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:22.560
This seems a bit more likely, since we know
the events of Doctor Strange in the Multiverse

00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:24.940
of Madness will tie into the events of the
series.

00:07:25.310 --> 00:07:28.560
But It could be that Wanda will travel to
another world, one in which her lost love

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:33.259
is alive, but that, in doing so, somehow upsets
the balance of the Multiverse, leading a certain

00:07:33.260 --> 00:07:34.479
good Doctor to intervene.

00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:38.100
We won't know for sure until the series drops,
but it has been confirmed that the show will

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:40.420
take place after the events of Avengers: Endgame.

00:07:40.620 --> 00:07:43.660
It won't be a terribly long wait to discover
how it will all shake out.

00:07:43.660 --> 00:07:47.860
WandaVision is slated to debut on Disney+
sometime in the spring of 2021.

00:07:48.940 --> 00:07:53.220
What If? is an alternate universe anthology
series which has run in various formats since

00:07:53.229 --> 00:07:57.930
1977, exploring how events may have unfolded
if crucial moments in the mainstream Marvel

00:07:57.930 --> 00:07:59.760
timeline had played out differently.

00:07:59.860 --> 00:08:03.800
It allowed readers to consider scenarios both
intriguing (What if Spider-Man had joined

00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:05.650
the Fantastic Four?) and unthinkable.

00:08:05.650 --> 00:08:08.840
We're talking, "What if Doctor Strange were
a disciple of Dormammu?"

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:13.389
Well, what it did for the comics, the Disney+
animated series What If? intends to do for

00:08:13.389 --> 00:08:14.100
the MCU.

00:08:14.320 --> 00:08:18.500
Like its comics counterpart, What If? will
have an anthology format, with each episode

00:08:18.500 --> 00:08:21.240
tackling one specific moment in the MCU timeline.

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:25.449
We know what you're thinking, what if Star-Lord
hadn't picked the exact wrong moment to cold-cock

00:08:25.449 --> 00:08:25.940
Thanos?

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:29.919
We can already tell you: Infinity War would
have been a heck of a lot shorter and less

00:08:29.920 --> 00:08:30.420
tragic.

00:08:30.420 --> 00:08:34.200
We'll have to wait to see what weirdness this
animated outing will have in store for us.

00:08:34.210 --> 00:08:38.839
We did get some definite hints about a few
possible scenarios during Marvel's 2019 Comic-Con

00:08:38.839 --> 00:08:43.789
panel, which not only set a Summer 2021 date
for the show, but revealed an impressive line-up

00:08:43.789 --> 00:08:46.120
of MCU talent set to lend their voices.

00:08:46.330 --> 00:08:50.500
They will be joined by Jeffrey Wright in the
central role of Uatu the Watcher, likely a

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:54.580
Rod Serling-like host for the anthology's
multiverse-spanning speculations.

00:08:55.360 --> 00:08:59.779
Rounding out the first batch of Disney+ limited
series will be Hawkeye, which will see Jeremy

00:08:59.780 --> 00:09:02.000
Renner reprise his role as the Avenging archer.

00:09:02.250 --> 00:09:05.980
The series' logo, which is heavily inspired
by the one used on the character's well-received

00:09:05.990 --> 00:09:10.420
recent comics run from Matt Fraction and David
Aja, was dropped on the San Diego Comic-Con

00:09:10.420 --> 00:09:10.920
crowd.

00:09:11.120 --> 00:09:14.720
Along with the reveal came the confirmation
of a long-standing rumor: that the series

00:09:14.721 --> 00:09:18.640
will see the debut of Kate Bishop, a young
protege who takes up the mantle of Hawkeye

00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:19.420
in the comics.

00:09:19.640 --> 00:09:23.380
The series is confirmed to take place after
the events of Avengers: Endgame, so it'll

00:09:23.380 --> 00:09:27.560
likely see Clint Barton adjusting to a world
in which his beloved family has returned from

00:09:27.560 --> 00:09:32.889
being dusted in the Decimation, and his trusted
ally Natasha Romanoff is no more, having sacrificed

00:09:32.889 --> 00:09:35.290
herself to further the Avengers' mission in
Endgame.

00:09:35.290 --> 00:09:39.380
While no plot details were announced, Renner
did share one little tidbit with the Comic-Con

00:09:39.380 --> 00:09:44.040
crowd which suggests that Barton's mentorship
of Bishop will be key to the series' narrative.

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:44.540
He dished:

00:09:44.660 --> 00:09:47.780
"I get to teach someone else how to be a superhero
without superpowers."

00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:51.480
Fans have been clamoring for this storyline
to make its way to the screen for some time,

00:09:51.490 --> 00:09:55.370
but they'll have to wait a bit longer to see
it come to fruition: Hawkeye is scheduled

00:09:55.370 --> 00:09:58.100
to debut on Disney+ in the fall of 2021.

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:03.240
Given his fantastic character arc over his
last several appearances, culminating with

00:10:03.250 --> 00:10:07.490
his decision to join the Guardians of the
Galaxy at the conclusion of Avengers: Endgame,

00:10:07.490 --> 00:10:10.699
speculation had been running high for some
time that Thor would be the first Avenger

00:10:10.700 --> 00:10:12.540
to land himself a fourth solo film.

00:10:12.810 --> 00:10:17.320
It was confirmed in July 2019 that it was
happening, with Thor: Ragnarok's Taika Waititi

00:10:17.339 --> 00:10:21.880
returning to direct, but at that month's San
Diego Comic-Con, further details were announced

00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:23.389
that shocked those in attendance.

00:10:23.389 --> 00:10:27.870
Specifically, the flick, now officially titled
Thor: Love and Thunder, releasing November

00:10:27.870 --> 00:10:33.029
5, 2021, will see the return of Natalie Portman's
Jane Foster, who will follow in her character's

00:10:33.029 --> 00:10:36.800
recent comic book footsteps by picking up
Mjolnir to become Thor herself.

00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:41.360
Tessa Thompson will also return as Valkyrie,
and Kevin Feige has confirmed that this time

00:10:41.360 --> 00:10:45.420
around, it will be made explicit that the
character is bisexual, a first for a major

00:10:45.420 --> 00:10:46.880
character in an MCU film.

00:10:47.180 --> 00:10:50.700
This, along with the flick's title, have led
some to speculate that the God of Thunder

00:10:50.700 --> 00:10:54.620
just might find himself in the middle of a
complicated love triangle, one involving two

00:10:54.620 --> 00:10:58.590
women who are just as powerful as he, and
who may prove to be slightly more interested

00:10:58.590 --> 00:11:00.060
in each other than they are in him.

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:04.959
So far, so awesome, but we just have one question:
is this a brand new Mjolnir, or the same one

00:11:04.960 --> 00:11:07.980
Captain America returned to 2013 in Avengers:
Endgame?

00:11:08.710 --> 00:11:10.680
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:11:10.700 --> 00:11:13.800
Plus, even more Looper videos about the MCU
are coming soon.

00:11:13.960 --> 00:11:17.800
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

